{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b01884855d25e956","name":"card_event_eagle_day","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WorldAtWar/events/card_event_eagle_day","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EAGLE DAY","text":"Put a German air unit into play with Blitz. Return it to your hand at the end of the turn.","flavorText":"Eagle Day (Adlertag) marked the first day of Operation Eagle Attack, (Unternehmen Adlerangriff), the codename of a military operation by the German Luftwaffe in 1940, with the intention of destroying the British Royal Air Force (RAF). This was done in preparation for Operation Sea Lion (Unternehmen Seelöwe), the German plan for the invasion of Britain, and the goal was to prevent the RAF from attacking the invasion fleet and to cripple the air defense of the Royal Navy Home Fleet. The operation was postponed several times due to bad weather, but was finally carried out on 13 August 1940. Hermann Göring, the commander in chief of the Luftwaffe, had promised Hitler that the RAF would be destroyed in a matter of days. However, the operation failed its objectives and the Germans never managed to gain air superiority in British airspace. This caused Operation Sea Lion to be postponed indefinitely.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_eagle_day","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_eagle_day_title","SourceString":"EAGLE DAY","LocalizedString":"EAGLE DAY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_eagle_day_text","SourceString":"Put a German air unit into play with Blitz. Return it to your hand at the end of the turn.","LocalizedString":"Put a German air unit into play with Blitz. Return it to your hand at the end of the turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_eagle_day_history","SourceString":"Eagle Day (Adlertag) marked the first day of Operation Eagle Attack, (Unternehmen Adlerangriff), the codename of a military operation by the German Luftwaffe in 1940, with the intention of destroying the British Royal Air Force (RAF). This was done in preparation for Operation Sea Lion (Unternehmen Seelöwe), the German plan for the invasion of Britain, and the goal was to prevent the RAF from attacking the invasion fleet and to cripple the air defense of the Royal Navy Home Fleet. The operation was postponed several times due to bad weather, but was finally carried out on 13 August 1940. Hermann Göring, the commander in chief of the Luftwaffe, had promised Hitler that the RAF would be destroyed in a matter of days. However, the operation failed its objectives and the Germans never managed to gain air superiority in British airspace. This caused Operation Sea Lion to be postponed indefinitely.","LocalizedString":"Eagle Day (Adlertag) marked the first day of Operation Eagle Attack, (Unternehmen Adlerangriff), the codename of a military operation by the German Luftwaffe in 1940, with the intention of destroying the British Royal Air Force (RAF). This was done in preparation for Operation Sea Lion (Unternehmen Seelöwe), the German plan for the invasion of Britain, and the goal was to prevent the RAF from attacking the invasion fleet and to cripple the air defense of the Royal Navy Home Fleet. The operation was postponed several times due to bad weather, but was finally carried out on 13 August 1940. Hermann Göring, the commander in chief of the Luftwaffe, had promised Hitler that the RAF would be destroyed in a matter of days. However, the operation failed its objectives and the Germans never managed to gain air superiority in British airspace. This caused Operation Sea Lion to be postponed indefinitely."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","waitWithOnOtherCardPlayedUntilHandTargetSelected":true,"selectHandCardNotifyText":{"Namespace":"","Key":"02A4B7AF404B2D